<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  `Info.plist` embedded into the helper executable (PR-042).

  NEVER EMBEDDED, NEVER READ BY macOS. This file is linked into the helper's
  `__TEXT,__info_plist` section by `apps/desktop/scripts/build-helper.js`, which
  has only ever run on Linux, where it stages a placeholder shell script and
  never invokes the linker.

  WHY IT EXISTS. A bare Mach-O executable has no bundle and therefore no usage
  strings. macOS *terminates* a process that asks for the microphone or for
  speech recognition without one — it is not a denial the process can handle,
  it is a crash. Whether that applies to `PilotHelper` depends entirely on
  whether TCC treats the app bundle or the helper as the requesting subject:

    · if the responsible process is `Pilot.app`, the app's own strings in
      `electron-builder.yml#mac.extendInfo` are used and this section is inert;
    · if the responsible process is the helper, this section is the only thing
      standing between a first push-to-talk and an immediate crash.

  It is cheap insurance against the case nobody here can test, which is why it
  is embedded by default and turned off with `--no-embed-info-plist` rather than
  the other way round.

  CFBundleIdentifier is a CHILD of the app's (`works.pilot.desktop.helper`),
  matching how Electron names its own helper processes. A completely unrelated
  identifier would guarantee a second TCC subject; reusing the app's identifier
  verbatim would put two differently-signed binaries behind one identity, which
  `codesign` and TCC both dislike.

  LSBackgroundOnly keeps the helper out of the Dock and out of the app switcher
  if macOS ever treats it as an application.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
    <string>works.pilot.desktop.helper</string>
    <key>CFBundleName</key>
    <string>PilotHelper</string>
    <key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
    <string>Pilot Helper</string>
    <key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
    <string>APPL</string>
    <key>CFBundleInfoDictionaryVersion</key>
    <string>6.0</string>
    <key>LSBackgroundOnly</key>
    <true/>
    <key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key>
    <string>13.0</string>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Pilot listens while you hold the push-to-talk key.</string>
    <key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Pilot turns what you say into text so it can answer.</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
